... Martin Literary Management and heads up adult fiction. Learn more.\\n\\nDigital media ventures\\n\\n- A new digital storytelling app, Alexander, focuses on shorts works by well-known authors. Alexander will launch with nonfiction works from authors such as Colum McCann, Xiaolu Guo, Chigozie Obioma, Carlo Rovelli, and Valeria Luiselli ... \",\"title\":\"https://janefriedman.com/new-publishers-agents-and-other-ventures-in-2020/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d137\"},\"ref\":\"d137\",\"snippet\":\" ... I, a great new African writer is asking these questions in a spare yet extraordinary novel about this bloody stain on human history.\\\"\\n\\n–Chigozie Obioma (The New York Times Book Review)\\n\\nFinalists:\\n\\nPeter Cameron, What Happens at Night (Catapult)\\n\\nAkwaeke Emezi, The Death of Vivek Oji (Riverhead)\\n\\nDanielle ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-award-winning-novels-of-2021/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d136\"},\"ref\":\"d136\",\"snippet\":\" ... BA, Harvard\\n\\nPhD, Yale\\n\\nShapiro Writing Center\\n\\nChigoze Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize. His novels have been translated into more than 30 languages. They have won awards including the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.wesleyan.edu/about/news/2023/09/wesleyan-welcomes-56-new-faculty-members-for-2023-24-academic-year.html\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"d478bac116583997857940a48ae8a289607d3b364b1737a9839355095ee290e9\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"6ad55d377bc6f9c14b29d2a