.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d138\"},\"ref\":\"d138\",\"snippet\":\" ... Long before the British, Nigeria suffered its first wave of colonialism by Arabs who wiped out cultures and instituted the Arabic way of life chiefly in Northern Nigeria. Within the arbitrary border drawn up by the British, the Nigeria of today contains multitudes. Be it in total number ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d135\"},\"ref\":\"d135\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\ndate: 2000-01-01\\n---\\n-\\n\\n- MajorsMinorsCertificates\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Policies & ProceduresFYW Guidebook\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Digital Learning LabsPortfoliosEvaluationsMoran ePortfolio AwardsBarnett Essay AwardsDouble Dawgs\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Transfer FAQProspective Student Information\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Study AbroadInternships and Research Opportunities\\n\\n>>\\n\\n-\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Double DawgsTransfer Student InformationDual Degree Progra\",\"title\":\"https://www.english.uga.edu/directory/people/chigozie-obioma\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d133\"},\"ref\":\"d133\",\"snippet\":\" ... Oromay (\\\"The End\\\")\\n* Chinua Achebe (Nigeria): Arrow of God (1964), No Longer At Ease (1960), Things Fall Apart (1958), A Man of the People (1966), Anthills of the Savannah (1987), \\n* Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie (Nigeria): Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d140\"},\"ref\":\"d140\",\"snippet\":\" ... Born and raised in Queenstown, in South Africa's Eastern Cape, he now resides in Cape Town, where he has continued to nurture a far-ranging knowledge of Xhosa history and culture. His first novel, The Broken River Tent, reconstitutes the perspective of a real-life 19th-century ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2021/03/the-xhosa-literary-revival\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d142\"},\"ref\":\"d142\",\"snippet\":\" ... Judith Van Allen notes that early ethnographic studies of Igbo communities comment on the 1929 Women's War in southeastern Nigeria, a protest that saw Igbo women challenge the policies of the colonial government. Rhonda Cobham's feminist reading says that while Achebe mentions the Women's Council ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Thing_Around_Your_Neck\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d137\"},\"ref\":\"d137\",\"snippet\":\" ... is a richly drawn and intimate portrait of 16th-century English life set against the arrival of one devastating death. O'Farrell, always a master of timing and rhythm, uses these flashbacks of young love and early marriage to heighten the sense of dread that accumulates as Hamnet ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-award-winning-novels-of-2021/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d152\"},\"ref\":\"d152\",\"snippet\":\" ... Alexander will launch with nonfiction works from authors such as Colum McCann, Xiaolu Guo, Chigozie Obioma, Carlo Rovelli, and Valeria Luiselli. It is subscription based ($3.99/month) and integrates audio performance and short film; readers can toggle between text and audio. Read the press release.\\n\\n- Binge Books ... \",\"title\":\"https://janefriedman.com/new-publishers-agents-and-other-ventures-in-2020/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"347e0293c0e51f2853ffca698df7364d1bf5b8f8da48966972190af9437e9af0\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"7cf7c00e7240aa4051c62e48f96909a645375582dda8609e9210d1c4484b76d9\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma early life Nigeria where raised\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_a470afab602d41009aef74e6"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle structure carefully. The puzzle says the award was \"originally created in the 2000s.\" The Man Booker International Prize was inaugurated in 2005 (the 2000s). \n\nBut there's a problem: The Fishermen (2015) was shortlisted for the **Booker Prize** (the main one, created 1968), not the International Booker Prize. So the puzzle's award can't be the Booker Prize.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about a different award entirely. Let me think about awards created in the 2000s:\n- Man Booker International Prize (2005)\n- The Story Prize (2004)\n- PEN/Faulkner Award (1980, no)\n- Walter Scott Prize (2010, no)\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether the puzzle might be about the International Booker Prize and a different book. The puzzle: Book A is a contender for an award created in the 2000s, translated into 25+ languages. In the 2010s, the year Book A was published, another book (Book B) won that award. Book B was released the preceding year. The author of Book B was born in the same city where the author of Book A grew up.\n\nWait — maybe Book A is NOT The Fishermen. Let me reconsider. The \"translated into over 25 languages\" + \"contender for an award created in the 2000s\" + \"in the 2010s, the year this book was published\" — these are strong constraints. Let me check the Man Booker International Prize 2015 winner (Krasznahorkai) and whether his winning book was released the preceding year (2014). And whether Krasznahorkai was born in the same city where Obioma grew up (Akure). That seems unlikely (Krasznahorkai is Hungarian).\n\nLet me reconsider — maybe the award is the International Booker Prize, and Book A is a book that was shortlisted/contender for it. Let me check the 2019 International Booker Prize, since An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) by Obioma was translated into 30+ languages. Was it a contender for the International Booker Prize? Actually, the International Booker Prize is for translated works. Let me check the 2019 International Booker Prize winner and shortlist.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize 2019 winner shortlist\", \"Man Booker International Prize 2019 winner\", \"An Orchestra of Minorities International Booker Prize contender\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_7c1c47638aed44529de03dee","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d143\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_19e30fd2a4534da187f333ae","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... List of winners and nominated authors of the Booker Prize - Wikipedia\\ndate: 2002-08-11\\n---\\nThe following is a list of winners and shortlisted authors of the Booker Prize for Fiction. The prize has been awarded each year since 1969 to the best original full-length novel, written ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... Man Booker Prize (2002–2019), is a prestigious literary award conferred each year for the best single work of sustained fiction written in the English language, which was published in the United Kingdom or Ireland. The winner of the Booker Prize receives , as well as international publicity that ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... Tonight, the Booker Foundation is reporting that the announcement of the 2021 International Booker Prize-winner, At Night All Blood Is Black, written by David Diop and translated by Anna Moschovakis, saw the book's publisher, Pushkin Press, order a five-figure reprint the day after the winner ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d81\"},\"ref\":\"d81\",\"snippet\":\" ... First, we confirmed that the Orange Prize drove long-term retention for its inaugural winner, Helen Dunmore's A Spell of Winter (which was also nominated for the Booker, but did not make the shortlist): compared to the median woman-authored novel in our data, A Spell of ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d83\"},\"ref\":\"d83\",\"snippet\":\" ... Man Booker Prize (longlist)\\n* 2014 California Book Awards Silver Medal Fiction winner for Orfeo\\n* 2018 Man Booker Prize (shortlist)\\n* 2019 Pulitzer Prize for Fiction\\n* 2019 PEN Oakland Josephine Miles Literary Award for The Overstory\\n* 2020 William Dean Howells Medal for The Overstory\\n* 2021 Booker Prize (shortlist)\\n* 2021 National ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Powers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... His last novel, Judas, was shortlisted for the Booker Prize in 2017 and won the Yasnaya Polyana Foreign Fiction Award. He received several international awards, including the Prix Femina, the Israel Prize, the Goethe Prize, the Frankfurt Peace Prize and the 2013 Franz Kafka Prize. He died in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d91\"},\"ref\":\"d91\",\"snippet\":\" ... The International Booker Prize 2023 Shortlist\\n\\nAt London Book Fair: Insights Into Translation Buyers\\n\\nAs the news of the International Booker Prize shortlist was announced to the public amid the raucous noise and crush of simultaneously programmed events at London Book Fair's opening today (April 17), the ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2023/04/london-book-fair-the-bookers-new-data-on-translation-buyers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d110\"},\"ref\":\"d110\",\"snippet\":\" ... when her longtime editor turned down her 2019 novel Ducks, Newburyport – one sentence, 1,000 pages long – she sent the manuscript to Sam Jordison and Eloise Millar of Norwich indie Galley Beggar Press; it promptly made the Booker shortlist and won the Goldsmiths prize for experimental fiction. No ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d153\"},\"ref\":\"d153\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2024-11-12\\n---\\nWe take a look at some of our favourite Booker Prize-winning novels and the nominees we love, including Percival Everett's James from this year's shortlist.\\n\\nWe take a look at some of our favourite winners and nominees of the revered Booker Prizes ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.panmacmillan.com/blogs/literary/our-all-time-favourite-man-booker-prize-winning-novels\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"2369fa5a5d435225ea2ae99fe38debf399b360042911ab987c3d6951c317e74a\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"ddf67d7fba88daf676d9ac1091519becac7865203e93f18c6ffb5bc95cb05331\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Booker Prize 2019 winner shortlist\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"pr